      "message": "johnstiles@ FYI this is a thing. This is not an issue for SkSL compute shaders (and to my knowledge the MSL generated by tint) since MSL codegen outputs local variables for `threadgroup` variables. IIUC the main use case for this is to dynamically resize of workgroup memory available to the shader.\n\nIn our use cases this can always be determined statically during shader/pipeline compilation. TBH, I think this is likely a bug in naga since WGSL requires workgroup variables to have a fixed footprint (see the table in https://www.w3.org/TR/WGSL/#var-and-value).",
